        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.093,
            0.744,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "so far away that they look like shining dots, just like stars. So how can we distinguish between planets and the stars? Unlike planets, the stars appear to twinkle a lot."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.166,
            0.488,
            0.189
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 12.4: Let us try to identify"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.199,
            0.559,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "With the help of an app, Venus can be located either at dawn or at dusk."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.246,
            0.528,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": " When you are viewing at dawn, look for it near the Eastern direction before sunrise."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.313,
            0.593,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": " When you are viewing at dusk, look for it near the Western direction after sunset."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.223,
            0.715,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": "How can we see the planets which are not visible to the naked eye?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.696,
            0.248,
            0.884,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.379,
            0.7,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "While many of the objects in the sky can be seen with our naked eyes directly, we can see them brighter and larger using a pair of binoculars or an instrument called a telescope (Fig. 12.8). A telescope also helps us view many dim objects not visible by our naked eyes directly."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.503,
            0.727,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "You may get an opportunity to view the sky through a telescope whenever a night sky watching event is organised in your region."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.607,
            0.443,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "Many Higher Education Institutions conduct night sky watching activities for school students. There are many Amateur Astronomy"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.708,
            0.406,
            0.888,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.49,
            0.639,
            0.67,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "We know that planets move around the Sun. Are there any objects that move around planets?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.744,
            0.23,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.711,
                0.637,
                0.883,
                0.656
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 12.8: A telescope"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.8,
            0.237,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": "**Do you know?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.71,
            0.5,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": "Clubs all over the country which organise sky watching events periodically. Museums and Planetariums also organise similar events."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.601,
            0.746,
            0.809,
